      "writtenOn": "2023-07-05T19:10:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apologies, I missed this important detail during my reviews. Since each port configuration has a unique ID, and different ports are used for remote submix input and output, matching between the ends of the pipe needs to be done using the device address, not port ID.\n\nIn the legacy implementation, the framework was simply opening input and output streams specifying the device address. In the AIDL, the framework must first call `setAudioPortConfig` to obtain a port config ID which is then passed to `openInput/OutputStream` method.",
